<p>Tuesday night just got better with these yummy takeout noodles. Yep, swi=
tching things up again this week and swapping out my usual <a title=3D"Pump=
kin Butter Chocolate Chip Cookies." href=3D"https://www.halfbakedharvest.co=
m/pumpkin-butter-chocolate-chip-cookies/" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener=
 noreferrer">sweet recipes</a> for something a bit more savory. Not typical=
 of me, but I was way too excited to share these Dan Dan inspired noodles w=
ith you guys.</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_1_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-a=
d adthrive-sticky-container adthrive-content adthrive-content-1"></div>
<p>First things first. I want to put it out there that I=E2=80=99m very wel=
l aware that these noodles are not authentic Chinese. I do know this, and I=
 don=E2=80=99t mean to offend anyone by sharing this recipe. This recipe is=
 just my take on Chinese style Dan Dan noodles. My easier, much, much simpl=
er, =E2=80=9Cshort cut=E2=80=9D take. These noodles are saucy, spicy, so ve=
ry warming, and beyond delicious.</p>
<p>Quick and easy enough for a weeknight, but fun enough for a Saturday nig=
ht Halloween movie marathon.</p>
<h3>Some background.</h3>
<p>If you=E2=80=99re not familiar with Dan Dan noodles, they are spicy Chin=
ese noodles with a dark sauce that usually contains preserved vegetables, c=
hili oil, minced pork (I=E2=80=99m using chicken), and green onions. From e=
verything I=E2=80=99ve read, the meat is caramelized and made crispy, then =
served over noodles. You can serve the noodles either dry or in a spicy bro=
th=E2=80=A6</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_2_desktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad =
adthrive-sticky-container adthrive-content adthrive-content-2"></div>
<p>I went for the spicy broth, because it=E2=80=99s been snowing here and i=
t=E2=80=99s cold. So spicy broth wins. Always.</p>
