<h3>Here are all the details on making these noodles.</h3>
<p>As I said, these are not authentic Dan Dan noodles. I took some short-cu=
ts to make the noodles weeknight-friendly, but still delicious.</p>
<p>Start with the chili. You can buy this of course, but I=E2=80=99ve yet t=
o find a great chili oil I love. Plus it=E2=80=99s so easy to make. Simply =
simmer sesame oil with garlic and red pepper flakes until the garlic is fra=
grant. This takes only five minutes. Simple.</p>
<p>While that=E2=80=99s happening, make the sauce. It=E2=80=99s s a simple =
mix of hoisin sauce, honey, rice vinegar, and peanut butter or tahini. Hois=
in is not traditional, but it adds so much flavor without having to add a m=
illion and one ingredients to the sauce.</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_4_d=
esktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad adthrive-sticky-container adthrive-content adt=
hrive-content-4"></div>
<p><em>Side Note:</em> I=E2=80=99ve yet to find a great hoisin sauce that d=
oesn=E2=80=99t contain tons of sugar=E2=80=A6so I began making my own. If t=
his interests you, the quick sauce mix-up is in the recipe notes!</p>
<p>Next, boil the egg noodles. You can really use any kind of noodle, but a=
 good egg noodle is probably best. If you are gluten-free, use your favorit=
e rice noodles. Those will be great too!</p>
<p>Drain the noodles, then add the broth and some of the sauce mix to that =
same pot. This is your =E2=80=9Cspicy broth=E2=80=9D to mix the noodles wit=
h. Keep this on low while you brown the chicken.</p>
<p>The final step is to brown the chicken in a skillet with the remaining s=
auce and mushrooms. Finely chop the mushrooms, as they add not only a veget=
able, but also flavor. You don=E2=80=99t even realize they=E2=80=99re there=
, but they add SO MUCH. Trust me.</p>
<p>Once the sauce coats the chicken, let the chicken get a little crisp in =
the skillet and begin to caramelize around the edges.</p>
<p>To assemble, ladle the spicy broth into bowls, add the noodles, and toss=
 with the broth. Then top with that crispy caramelized meat, spoon over add=
itional chili sauce, and add fresh green onions.</p>
<p>Find a spoon, find chopsticks. ENJOY.</p><div id=3D"AdThrive_Content_5_d=
esktop" class=3D"adthrive-ad adthrive-sticky-container adthrive-content adt=
hrive-content-5"></div>
